# Cloud tiers — the offer

The companion to the pricing comparison directly above: having shown *we don't bill per seat*, this
section shows **what you actually choose** — how big a machine, and how much storage. Every tier is
the whole product (every feature, unlimited people); the only thing that changes up the ladder is
the size of the machine and the room it has for your data.

There is **no free tier** — a nexus is a real machine — but the floor is an uber-cheap hook (**Solo,
$12**) on the smallest machine, then **Studio ($32)** is the genuine sweet spot. Pricing works
because the machine *suspends when idle* (you feel always-on; we only pay Fly for the seconds it
runs) and the database is SQLite-by-default (zero marginal) with Postgres on-demand. Numbers are
margin-checked against real Fly + Neon + R2 cost at scale-to-zero; the canonical enforced tiers live
in the deploy manifest `dogfood/index.work` (read by `Nexus.Config.tiers`), which this section mirrors.
(The old `deployment.work` fallback is retired — see `nexus/lib/config.ex`.) Accents rotate
the DNA pastels (sky · mint · peach · lilac), never the neon primary.

client :tiers do
